</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">;;; </span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">treats the mantissa as a fraction [0.5, 1.0). In practice this means that
</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">;;; </span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">exponents in our canonical representation must be recalculated, because:
</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">;;;</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">
</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">;;;   </span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">our-mantissa === (shift-to-odd (ash float-mantissa +ldbl-mant-dig+))
</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">;;;   </span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">our-min-exp  === (- +ldbl-min-exp+ +ldbl-mant-dig+)
</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">;;;   </span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">our-max-exp  === (- +ldbl-max-exp+ (integer-length our-mantissa))
</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">;;;</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">
</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">;;; </span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">Note that FLOAT-MANTISSA assumes a fraction, but in practice we can usually
</span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">;;; </span><span style="color: #7f7f7f;">extract bits directly and skip the shift by interpreting it as significand.
</span>(<span style="color: #00bfff;">defun</span> <span style="color: #daa520;">hash-dyadic-number</span> (state number)
