<ul class="org-ul">
<li>bignum decision cost boils down to counting trailing zeros, the dyadic hash
operates in a register and it doesn't cons</li>

<li>ratio decision cost is optimized to not perform bignum arithmetic, so the
decision cost is negligible and the main cost is in hashing long double</li>

<li>float creates an integer from the mantissa - in most cases it is a fixnum,
otherwise it operates on a bignum register and it doesn't cons either</li>
</ul>

